{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TCwG5kZZPn5Dd12635yjdY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment using Unix utilities as a test bed. It derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations from those specs using an AI coding agent, and verifies parity via differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline: extract → specify → synthesize → verify. Key components: cmd/ (utilities), pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils, magefiles/, docs/specs/.\n\n**Current State**: This is generation-run44. Looking at the code_status in the analysis, I need to identify which use cases have `codestatus: not started` vs `codestatus: implemented`.\n\n\nNow I'm checking the requirement_states to see which specs are ready for implementation. Only four utilities from release 15.0 have all their requirements marked as ready: ts, stty, pr, and ptx. But there are many use cases across earlier releases that haven't been started yet, so I need to map out which releases have incomplete work. I'm continuing through the remaining utility implementations, with several more test cases across different releases still waiting to be started—including mktemp, groups, sort, mv, sleep, factor, and various checksum utilities. I'm realizing the constraint means I can only propose tasks for the four utilities that have entries in requirement_states—srd004-ts, srd105-stty, srd110-pr, and srd111-ptx—since those are the only ones with R-items marked as \"ready\". Everything else falls outside the scope of what I can suggest. I need to work with what I have since I can't read the requirements.yaml file directly. The constraint specifies that each requirement has a weight field with a default of 1, so I'll assume default weights unless